        } ],
        "parts" : [ {
          "name" : "overview",
          "prose" : "# Further information\n\nFurther information on secure network design can be found in ASD’s [Foundations for modern defensible architecture](#8a67ffd7-61a4-4773-a1e7-e6b146f51d62) publication.\n\nFurther information on wired networks can be found in the ‘Wired networks’ section of these guidelines.\n\nFurther information on wireless networks can be found in the ‘Wireless networks’ section of these guidelines.\n\nFurther information on gateways can be found in the ‘Gateways’ section of the [Guidelines for gateways](#e8bde527-526c-4a6a-b66f-05228f09dd7b).\n\nFurther information on encrypting communications can be found in the ‘Cryptographic fundamentals’ section of the [Guidelines for cryptography](#195abe87-bb1e-4006-8b42-eaecca4d51f1).\n\nFurther information on network segmentation and segregation can be found in ASD’s [Implementing network segmentation and segregation](#23d977b2-e64e-4ebc-a59f-cd95212045c5) publication.\n\nFurther information on network security zones can be found in Canada’s Canadian Centre for Cyber Security’s [Baseline security requirements for network security zones (version 2.0)](#b43b0377-c2e4-4cdc-acec-a9ece7371e36) publication.\n\nFurther information on implementing network segmentation and segregation for system administration purposes can be found in the ‘System administration’ section of the [Guidelines for system management](#c6ca6620-ccd5-4c5d-b97c-9d92f1162948).\n\nFurther information on functional separation of servers using virtualisation can be found in the ‘Virtualisation hardening’ section of the [Guidelines for system hardening](#de7525f3-a466-40a5-abdd-3ae24a6d1b44).\n\nFurther information on cyber supply chain risk management can be found in the ‘Cyber supply chain risk management’ section of the [Guidelines for procurement and outsourcing](#f37a4848-0791-4870-b316-5536c2681c28).\n\nFurther information on evaluated products can be found in the ‘Evaluated product procurement’ section of the [Guidelines for evaluated products](#a699a3aa-828d-479b-b50b-98127bb19437).\n\nFurther information on blocking anonymity network traffic can be found in ASD’s [Defending against the malicious use of the Tor network](#ded13757-3c76-40cb-b46e-f84e46a1c1c7) publication.\n\nFurther information on DNS services can be found in ASD’s [Domain Name System security for domain owners](#b66f8d23-4209-4775-a1fd-bd4dc299a027) and [Domain Name System security for domain resolvers](#b13cb68a-a94a-4a69-b094-b1b68d10239e) publications.\n\nFurther information on implementing encrypted DNS can be can be found in the United States’ National Security Agency’s [Adopting Encrypted DNS in Enterprise Environments](#e2205e57-2bf0-4696-8bd8-94a5a5d5c4f2) publication and the Cybersecurity \\& Infrastructure Security Agency’s [Encrypted DNS Implementation Guidance](#fba4bdb9-82be-47a4-8198-3d47d5786932) publication.\n\nFurther information on selecting a protective DNS service can be found in the United States’ National Security Agency and Cybersecurity \\& Infrastructure Security Agency’s [Selecting a Protective DNS Service](#63b0d043-b6b3-4e2b-bca8-99b42cfd9904) publication.\n\nFurther information on network device hardening, particularly for internet-facing network devices, can be found in the following publications:\n\n- ASD’s [Mitigation strategies for edge devices: Executive guidance](#b79c4fe8-4541-401f-a32e-87fd83021c98)\n- ASD’s [Mitigation strategies for edge devices: Practitioner guidance](#0cae2aee-3762-482f-8ffe-850e98d7d605)\n- Canada’s Canadian Centre for Cyber Security’s [Security considerations for edge devices](#c47ab307-e25d-43e7-9700-7b26d9c229c3)\n- United Kingdom’s National Cyber Security Centre’s [Guidance on digital forensics and protective monitoring specifications for producers of network devices and appliances](#53d281fa-1f25-4d33-9d6b-a5831851df50).\n\nFurther information on network device hardening can also be found in the United States’ National Security Agency’s [Network Infrastructure Security Guide](#1ecfc41e-f6a8-4c96-ac41-1587718ca459) publication.\n\nFurther information on event logging can be found in the ‘Security monitoring’ section of the [Guidelines for security assurance](#ef60c0e4-acfb-4a8b-b5ed-25675c6e117c).\n\nFurther information on event logging for network devices can also be found in ASD’s [Priority logs for SIEM ingestion: Practitioner guidance](#1dbda98a-4e8b-4a52-b4f7-9d1a895fd324) publication."
        } ],
        "groups" : [ {
          "title" : "Network documentation",
          "props" : [ {
            "name" : "sort-id",
            "value" : "catalog[1].group[22].group[1].group[01]"
          } ],
          "parts" : [ {
            "name" : "overview",
            "prose" : "It is important that accurate and sufficiently detailed network documentation is developed as this can assist in troubleshooting network problems as well as responding to and recovering from cyber security incidents. As such, network documentation should include high-level network diagrams showing all connections into networks; logical network diagrams showing all critical servers, high-value servers, network devices and network security appliances; and device settings for all critical servers, high-value servers, network devices and network security appliances. Finally, as network documentation could be used by malicious actors to assist in compromising networks, it is important that it is appropriately protected."
          } ],
